If `socket.peer_addr()` fails, `remote_addr` will be `None`, causing the SourceIp to default to '127.0.0.1' in policy evaluation. This could allow unauthorized access if a policy denies the default IP or allows only specific IPs. Consider logging the failure or handling it more explicitly to avoid security issues.
```suggestion
        let remote_addr = match socket.peer_addr() {
            Ok(addr) => Some(RemoteAddr(addr)),
            Err(e) => {
                tracing::warn!(
                    error = %e,
                    "Failed to obtain peer address; policy evaluation may fall back to a default source IP"
                );
                None
            }
        };
```
